      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}: ok, then leave very good as is, and just change the others. My avatar is optimized as much as possible and i can get medium or even good (bc of unique materials, i'd have to atlas even more) if i don't use dynamic bones. I just think, that the amounts of dynamic bones i specified up top would be ok. I've seen people with over 150 dynamic bone transforms and they don't lag my game by a significant margin. Tho I do understand, that there are people with worse hardware and it may be difficult for them. But on such systems it would be more useful to completely disable dynamic bones to increase fps instead of calling a avatar poorly optimized, that just has a few.. :/",
      "viewerReactions": null
